      "ingredients": "Ingredients\nFor the Steak:\n1 slab Clayton Organic Steak\n2 tbsps. whole black peppercorns, coarsely crushed\nSalt to taste\n2 tbsps. vegetable oil\n2 tbsps. unsalted butter\nFor the Red Wine Sauce:\n1/2 cup red wine (such as Cabernet Sauvignon or Merlot)\n1/2 cup beef stock\n1 tbsp. Dijon mustard\n1 tbsp. unsalted butter \n1 shallot, finely chopped\n1 tbsps. parsley, chopped",
      "procedure": "Procedure\nTake the Clayton Organic Steak out of the refrigerator about 30 minutes before cooking to bring it to room temperature. Season both sides generously with salt black pepper.\nIn a large skillet, heat vegetable oil over medium-high heat. Sear the steak for about 4 minutes on one side until a crust forms. Flip the steak and add butter to the pan. Cook for an additional 3-4 minutes for medium-rare, adjusting time based on your preferred doneness.\nRemove the steak from the skillet and transfer it to a plate. Cover with foil, and let it rest while you prepare the sauce.\nIn the same skillet, reduce heat to medium and add chopped shallots. Sauté for about 2 minutes until softened. Deglaze with red wine, scraping up any browned bits from the bottom of the pan. Let it simmer for about 3 minutes, then add beef stock and Dijon mustard. Continue to simmer until slightly thickened, about 5 minutes. Stir in butter and parsley at the end.\nSlice the rested steak against the grain, and drizzle with red wine sauce. Serve with you preferred starch."
